**How the script works** (self-contained, git+coreutils only, no prompts, cwd-independent):
1. Recovers generically: enumerates unreachable objects via `git fsck --no-reflogs --unreachable`, plus sweeps every object in the ODB (`cat-file --batch-all-objects`), extracting `secret[...]` tokens; requires exactly one, writes it to `/app/secret.txt`.
2. Purges: `git reflog expire --expire=now --expire-unreachable=now --all`, removes `ORIG_HEAD`, `git worktree prune`, then `git gc --prune=now` (packs survivors, prunes all unreachable loose objects), with a fallback that deletes any remaining loose object still containing the marker and re-gcs.
3. Verifies its own gates and exits non-zero if any fail.

