Fix: /app/bank.py now uses a single global threading.Lock held for the entire duration of each operation — the whole transfer (funds check, debit, credit) and the whole balances() snapshot. One lock acquired in exactly one place per operation means no lock-ordering cycles, so no deadlock is possible; the atomic check-and-apply prevents overdrafts; and the snapshot copy happens under the same lock, so in-flight transfers can never be observed half-applied (no money "in flight" visible to balances()).

